# Purpose
One page an agent can read to use the org brain, org tasks, to-dos,
schedules, sprints and projects correctly. The how-to guides stay
people-first and link here.

# Sanitization
Rewrite-only from the agent tool schemas, the task list's contract and its
lifecycle rules. Tool names, input names and the error codes agents receive
are public (agents see them in tool results). No services, hosts, routes,
repositories, release numbers or internal ids.

# Gotchas (keep these true)
- The op table follows the engine lifecycle: block, skip and reopen need a
  reason; submit needs in progress (a private to-do may submit from open);
  approve is people only; accept and cancel are the only steps on a proposal.
- The completion record: AI, AI-then-human and script submits need the turn
  card as evidence; AI-then-human approve needs a person's summary; a human
  task in a sprint needs a summary, which agents send as `outcome` on
  submit. `outcome` only rides with op submit or approve.
- Schedules: notify {remindBefore, escalateAfter} durations ("2h", never
  "1d": Go durations have no day unit); escalate1 goes to assignee, queue
  and creator, escalate2 (org scope, at twice the delay) to managers;
  delivery is an open dashboard only. AI schedules need kind + instructions;
  human/script must have neither. Nodes not updated refuse the new fields.
- Ids: tools need full ids; cards show short ones, which answer not_found.
- Performer, run node and snooze changes are Agenda-only; the agent tools
  do not expose them.
- AI work starts only through an explicit run: Run now (`org_task_run` or
  the Agenda), a confirmed Run at due, an accepted AI schedule's run
  authority, or a current owner/admin brain mandate. A due time alone never
  starts work, script tasks never run, and a queued reply is not proof a
  worker started. Never promise an unrun task "will run".
- org_brain_ask: question up to 50,000 characters, mode org/open/web, model,
  depth quick/deep. org_brain_note: charter and guidance kinds need an org
  owner/admin (or platform support role); guidance needs scope, scopeId
  (not for org) and expiresAt within 30 days.
- Questions: 1-4 choices plus an engine-added decline (2-4 total), default
  expiry 168h (1h-720h); an open, declined or expired question locks its
  subject until a proceed answer.
- Task-run sessions (a run started by the run service) read and report on
  their own task only; other org reads, brain note reads, cross-node search,
  task creation and delegation answer authorization_denied. The run service
  attaches the result card and submits.

# Change History
- 2026-11-26: Run authority replaces "AI tasks never run"; adds org_task_run,
  questions, ask mode/model/depth, charter/guidance notes, task-run sessions; checked against the live agent tool schemas.
- 2026-11-14: outcome on org_task_update, schedule notify/kind/instructions, full ids (after the schedule fields fix).
- 2026-11-14: Created.
- 2026-11-26: task runs can read brain notes and write fact, decision, intent and finding notes; charter, guidance and deletes stay refused.
- 2026-11-27: org policy is on from the start (owner steward, every kind, no limits, revoke stays revoked); questions go to the org brain first (friendly agent, via brain, 4 h default). Merge at release of the default policy and friendly agent branches.
